implementationPlan.description:
The ps1 twin of step 2, in scripts/moe-agent.ps1:
- the remote L9 arm and its porcelain classification;
- Resolve-MoePushOutcome;
- the unknown-outcome handling: journal pushResult 'push unknown: …', a push-unknown rescue through Invoke-MoeRescueRef, no completion row, no finalize;
- L10 after a confirmed publication, and pushed: true only then;
- the round-ending reasons;
- the Invoke-MoeReceiptReplay worktree arm: fetch first, and receipt_landed_as's twin run against refs/remotes/origin/<target>.

Never call Push-MoeBranch for a worktree completion, and never read MOE_PUSH_REBASE on that path. Use the same codes and the same optional journal field as the sh twin.

Error handling, as in step 2: an ambiguous push or fetch answer never publishes, never mirrors and never finalizes.

planningNotes.codebaseInsights:
- Existing helpers to reuse:
  - no_git_remote (sh:5004) / Test-MoeNoRemote (ps1:4307) for the mode test;
  - receipt_journal_write, receipt_landed_as and receipt_replay (sh around 5307-5480);
  - Invoke-MoeReceiptReplay (ps1:1955);
  - rescue_ref (sh:4930) / Invoke-MoeRescueRef (ps1:4204).
- push_branch (sh:5035) / Push-MoeBranch (ps1:4317) hold the MOE_PUSH_REBASE retry. They must stay out of the worktree arm.
- GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 is already exported globally (sh:9, ps1:403).
- CI's Linux postflight step and the two Windows postflight steps sit around ci.yml lines 268-283.
